Write an assembly code that implements the following C program, which includes
addition and subtraction operations using appropriate addressing methods.
int X[] = {3, 12, 7, 1, 9};
int Y[] = {4, 10, 8, 5, 3};
int Z[5];
int i;
for(i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
if (X[i] + Y[i] > 15) {
Z[i] = 1;
}
else {
Z[i] = 0;
}
}
When converting this program to assembly language, please follow these guidelines:
Store arrays X and Y in the address ranges 80H-84H and 90H-94H, respectively.
At the end of your program, store the resulting array Z in the address range
A0H-A4H.
Place your machine code starting from memory address 200H.
